WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.760
Hi, I'm Briana from freeCodeCamp.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:03.980
Let's quick review.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.060
The four basic parts 
of a computer are:

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.740
the Input–like the mouse 
or the keyboard

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.300
The Output– what you're 
seeing on the monitor

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.700
or hearing through
 the speakers

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.380
the CPU– the 
Central Processing Unit

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.200
and the Memory.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.580
Now Memory can be short-term 
memory called RAM

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.860
or longer term memory. 
That is usually is a hard drive,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.240
but can also be like 
a CD-ROM or Flash Drive

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.240
anything like that.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.460
In addition to those 
four basic parts,

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.560
we have three more things 
we're going to discuss today.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.300
The Motherboard, Expansion Cards, 
and Power Supply.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.040
The Motherboard is what 
connects everything.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.980
While the data is flying 
around over here

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.040
trying to figure out 
where to go,

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.000
the Motherboard 
helps route it.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.260
So it goes to the 
right place.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.860
Expansion cards are 
sound cards, video cards,

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.380
that kind of thing that 
can really up your experience

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.140
as a user.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.580
Power supply is 
as it sounds–

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.509
what gets power 
to the computer.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.280
It's usually the part of the 
computer that has that fan on

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.840
it to keep it from overheating.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.100
So let's do a quick review.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.840
In addition to the 
four basic parts of

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.100
Input/Output, Central Processing Unit, 
and Memory

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.140
We usually have a 
Motherboard, Expansion Cards,

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.420
and a Power Supply.

